WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:19.120
The first day of this Satipatthana course is over.

00:19.120 --> 00:34.360
And the technique remains the same, your practice remains the same.

00:34.360 --> 00:49.920
But the course is a special course in the sense that you will try to understand the

00:49.920 --> 01:12.080
words of the enlightened one, the Buddha, with reference to the technique.

01:12.080 --> 01:34.120
Words of Buddha or words of Buddha, a fully enlightened person, every word is so enlightening,

01:34.120 --> 01:56.800
full of wisdom, every discourse of Buddha is so sweet, so precious.

01:56.800 --> 02:14.360
All the teachings of Buddha, all the discourses of Buddha, they are like a big sweet cake.

02:14.360 --> 02:29.960
Whichever portion you cut and eat, you get the same taste, the taste of nectar, ambrosia.

02:29.960 --> 02:40.680
But we have chosen specially this discourse because it deals with the technique that you

02:40.680 --> 02:50.520
are practicing in detail.

02:50.520 --> 03:09.460
It is better that the serious old students try to understand the technique, listening

03:09.460 --> 03:24.540
to the actual words of the Buddha himself, to understand what he wanted us to do and

03:24.540 --> 03:29.640
what we are doing.

03:29.640 --> 03:45.480
To understand the theoretical aspect of the practice more clearly, in more detail.

03:45.480 --> 03:55.400
And to come out of any confusion that one might have developed pertaining to the technique.

03:55.400 --> 04:08.360
Unfortunately this has happened in some cases, big confusion.

04:08.360 --> 04:23.400
A few students, having taken a few courses, out of their enthusiasm, started teaching

04:23.760 --> 04:35.040
without getting proper training, without going in the subject deeply.

04:35.040 --> 04:42.060
And they started mixing so many things with the technique.

04:42.060 --> 04:51.300
It happened in the West, it also happened in India.

04:51.300 --> 05:07.180
In India, mostly by such people who had great attachment to their own sectarian views.

05:07.180 --> 05:13.180
But they had no technique of meditation.

05:13.180 --> 05:20.860
They just attended a few courses, had a superficial knowledge of the technique and then started

05:20.860 --> 05:30.160
teaching it, giving it a colour of their own belief, sectarian, philosophical belief.

05:30.160 --> 05:35.620
And mixing up so many things.

05:35.620 --> 05:43.360
And when some of the Vipassana students go to them and take a course with them, they

05:43.360 --> 05:46.800
get very much confused.

05:46.800 --> 05:51.660
Because here is a student of Goenka who has taken courses in Vipassana and he has started

05:51.660 --> 05:54.140
teaching now.

05:54.140 --> 05:56.740
And look what he is teaching.

05:56.740 --> 06:00.380
Is this right or is that right?

06:00.380 --> 06:04.020
Great confusion.

06:04.020 --> 06:08.820
Such things have happened in the West also.

06:08.840 --> 06:16.800
In the West a big confusion is the reason that people who are teaching in their own

06:16.800 --> 06:26.160
way or we can say in different way, having the base of this technique, just to differentiate

06:26.160 --> 06:37.200
they will say what we are teaching is Satipatthana and what you practice with Goenka is Vipassana.

06:37.260 --> 06:41.260
A big confusion.

06:41.260 --> 06:44.500
Satipatthana is Vipassana.

06:44.500 --> 06:52.500
Vipassana is Satipatthana.

06:52.500 --> 07:00.060
To get things clarified and not only that.

07:00.080 --> 07:19.160
To understand Dhamma at a deeper level, relating it to the words, the direct words of the Buddha

07:19.260 --> 07:34.660
gives so much of inspiration, gives guidance as to how we should practice.

07:34.660 --> 07:43.020
Therefore the technique will remain the same but the evening discourses will be different.

07:43.020 --> 07:50.320
Here we will go through this Satipatthana Satya discourse, a very important discourse

07:50.320 --> 08:02.440
given by Buddha on this subject in detail.

08:02.440 --> 08:10.080
There are three aspects of Dhamma.

08:10.140 --> 08:16.520
We can say three important steps of Dhamma.

08:16.520 --> 08:24.560
The first is called Pariyatti.

08:24.560 --> 08:36.720
Understand during these eight days you will be hearing a number of Pali words.

08:36.720 --> 08:45.660
They will look very new to you but slowly you will start understanding them and later

08:45.660 --> 08:54.960
on a time will come when you will be able to develop even just a working knowledge of

08:54.960 --> 09:02.680
this language, the ancient language spoken by the Buddha.

09:02.680 --> 09:08.400
Then you will find every word is so inspiring.

09:08.400 --> 09:14.880
If you develop just the working language, working knowledge of the language and if you

09:14.880 --> 09:24.080
are a good Vipassana meditator you will notice that as you go through the words of Buddha

09:24.080 --> 09:32.200
it will look as if these words are said for me.

09:32.200 --> 09:39.200
Buddha himself is directing me, is telling me how to practice.

09:39.200 --> 09:48.480
Every word will be so inspiring for you but this is a beginning stage.

09:48.480 --> 09:52.620
Understand few words which will be helpful.

09:52.620 --> 10:04.020
The three steps, first Pariyatti.

10:04.020 --> 10:24.120
This is adequate knowledge, sufficient knowledge of the teaching at the intellectual level.

10:24.120 --> 10:42.460
One has heard something, one has read something, the words of the enlightened person, Pariyatti.

10:42.460 --> 10:58.820
One who has heard the words of the enlightened person is called a Sutva, Sutva, in Pali Sutva.

10:58.820 --> 11:10.880
One was heard, one was not heard at all.

11:10.900 --> 11:16.660
So difficult for this person to understand what Dhamma is.

11:16.660 --> 11:22.940
For this person Dhamma will be just a sectarian belief, a sectarian philosophical belief.

11:22.940 --> 11:29.140
Maybe a rite, maybe a ritual, maybe a ceremony, a religious ceremony and the whole life this

11:29.140 --> 11:38.640
person will remain involved in these things without understanding what Dhamma is.

11:38.640 --> 11:45.840
Because he never had an opportunity to hear the words of the enlightened person, read

11:45.840 --> 11:49.800
the words of the enlightened person.

11:49.800 --> 11:54.420
He can never understand.

11:54.420 --> 12:00.440
Because he has never heard even, he won't understand that Dhamma is universal.

12:00.440 --> 12:03.100
For him Dhamma will be just a religion.

12:03.560 --> 12:10.240
Oh this is Buddhist religion or this is Hindu religion or this is a Christian religion or

12:10.240 --> 12:16.120
a Muslim religion or a Jewish religion.

12:16.120 --> 12:21.840
Dhamma will be understood by this person only in this way.

12:21.840 --> 12:33.000
But if he has heard what Dhamma is, then he will understand Dhamma is law, Dhamma is truth.

12:33.900 --> 12:45.220
Dhamma is nature, the natural law which is universal.

12:45.220 --> 12:55.140
It cannot remain limited to a particular sect, a particular community.

12:55.280 --> 13:04.680
It is applicable on one and all, the law of nature, universal.

13:04.680 --> 13:13.640
Therefore Sutva is a very fortunate person who has at least heard what Dhamma is, who

13:13.640 --> 13:24.240
has at least heard how to practice Dhamma, who has at least heard how to apply Dhamma

13:24.340 --> 13:26.380
in life.

13:26.380 --> 13:37.460
A fortunate person compared to one who is a Sutva who has never heard, never heard anything

13:37.460 --> 13:47.740
about the truth, the universal truth, the natural truth.

13:47.740 --> 13:55.460
This person remains confused because he has never heard even.

13:55.460 --> 14:04.700
One who has heard is certainly a fortunate person compared to one who has never heard.

14:05.660 --> 14:24.980
But merely hearing or merely reading the words of an enlightened person is not enough.

14:24.980 --> 14:29.820
It is very good to give inspiration.

14:29.940 --> 14:42.620
It is very good to give you guidance so that you start practicing, but you don't practice.

14:42.620 --> 14:54.380
You feel quite satisfied having heard, you feel quite satisfied having read it, then

14:54.940 --> 15:08.740
it just becomes a devotional game for you, a devotional satisfaction which may even become

15:08.740 --> 15:15.680
a hindrance for your liberation.

15:15.680 --> 15:23.620
You feel so satisfied having heard the words of pure Dhamma, having read the words of pure

15:23.860 --> 15:33.540
Dhamma, you feel so satisfied, now I know everything.

15:33.540 --> 15:50.180
But actually you don't know, you just accepted the truth because you never practiced it.

15:50.740 --> 16:07.780
For every Sutva, everyone who has heard the words of pure Dhamma must start practicing.

16:07.780 --> 16:15.020
And for this the word is Patipatti.

16:15.020 --> 16:26.660
First was Pariyatti, a sufficient intellectual knowledge of Dhamma is Pariyatti.

16:26.660 --> 16:37.740
Then Patipatti, you start practicing it, the practice of Dhamma.

16:37.740 --> 16:41.180
As you might have heard in daily chantings,

16:41.180 --> 17:05.820
The Sangha which is Savaka, Savaka is a Sutva, the Sangha who has heard the teaching of Buddha

17:05.820 --> 17:16.500
and now they start walking on the path, Su Patipanno, they walk on the path properly.

17:16.500 --> 17:22.400
It is the walking on the path which will take you to the final goal, to your destination

17:22.400 --> 17:28.220
of full liberation, full enlightenment.

17:28.220 --> 17:41.260
Patipatti, Pariyatti alone cannot take you to the final goal.

17:41.260 --> 17:53.220
By Pariyatti, by listening Dhamma, one starts understanding, yes I must live the life of

17:53.220 --> 18:04.460
Dhamma, I must live the life of morality, I am a human being and a human being is a

18:04.460 --> 18:15.100
social being, one has to live in the society, one has to live with the members of the family.

18:15.100 --> 18:18.860
How to live?

18:18.860 --> 18:28.580
One should not disturb the peace and harmony of the people around.

18:28.580 --> 18:34.300
How can I experience peace and harmony if I keep on disturbing the peace and harmony

18:34.300 --> 18:36.780
of others?

18:36.780 --> 18:51.380
Therefore I should not perform any action, physical or vocal, which hurts and harms

18:51.380 --> 18:52.580
other beings.

18:52.580 --> 18:58.360
I should not perform such action.

18:58.360 --> 19:02.400
I should abstain from killing.

19:02.400 --> 19:06.100
I should abstain from stealing.

19:06.100 --> 19:11.260
I should abstain from sexual misconduct.

19:11.260 --> 19:26.180
I should abstain from speaking lies, speaking harsh words, speaking words of backbiting,

19:26.180 --> 19:31.460
speaking useless words, meaningless words, wasting my time, wasting time of others.

19:31.540 --> 19:35.500
I must abstain from that.

19:35.500 --> 19:42.140
I must abstain from taking any kind of intoxicants.

19:42.140 --> 19:46.660
One understands that.

19:46.660 --> 19:53.860
And one also understands, if one tries to understand the words of an enlightened person,

19:53.860 --> 20:08.580
one also understands that by abstaining such unwholesome actions, I am not obliging others.

20:08.580 --> 20:12.820
I am actually obliging myself.

20:12.820 --> 20:19.140
Because every time I perform any unwholesome action, physical or vocal, which goes against

20:19.140 --> 20:28.580
the interest of others, I cannot perform such actions unless I generate tremendous

20:28.580 --> 20:41.500
amount of impurity in my mind, craving, greed, hatred, aversion, ego, fear, some impurity

20:41.500 --> 20:43.700
or the other.

20:43.740 --> 20:51.900
And then only I perform vocal actions or physical actions which are unwholesome.

20:51.900 --> 20:56.860
And when I generate impurity in my mind, I have started harming myself.

20:56.860 --> 21:05.100
Oh, for this reason, I must live a life of morality.

21:05.100 --> 21:08.820
Sheila is very important for me.

21:08.820 --> 21:13.020
One understands that.

21:13.020 --> 21:23.020
But then, for patti-patti, for the actual practice, it becomes difficult.

21:23.020 --> 21:32.620
Because unless one has control over one's own mind, one cannot abstain from such unwholesome

21:32.620 --> 21:39.820
actions in spite of the fact that one understands at the intellectual level that such actions

21:39.820 --> 21:43.380
are no good for me, no good for others.

21:43.380 --> 21:49.660
And yet, because one has no mastery over the mind, one keeps on performing such unwholesome

21:49.660 --> 22:04.140
actions, therefore one learns how to control the mind.

22:04.140 --> 22:12.220
For Sheila, one practices samadhi.

22:12.220 --> 22:19.280
For some time under certain circumstances, in certain environments, like you come to

22:19.280 --> 22:27.900
a course because of the environment around you and because of the program from morning

22:27.900 --> 22:32.940
till night 9, 9.30, you are kept busy.

22:32.940 --> 22:34.860
You are not breaking any of the Sheila.

22:34.860 --> 22:42.220
But then, you have to develop the mastery over the mind.

22:42.220 --> 22:54.020
And you start practicing samadhi, patti-patti, su patti-panno.

22:54.020 --> 23:00.700
You started walking on the path.

23:00.700 --> 23:04.580
The second important section of dhamma.

23:04.580 --> 23:10.220
First is pariyatti, the theoretical knowledge of dhamma.

23:10.220 --> 23:15.180
The second is patti-patti.

23:15.180 --> 23:28.080
But as one proceeds on the path, properly, as an enlightened person wants you to proceed,

23:28.080 --> 23:32.520
you can control your mind in different ways.

23:32.520 --> 23:38.680
But if you have not controlled the mind in a proper way, then this controlling of the

23:38.680 --> 23:42.700
mind will not take you to the third step.

23:42.700 --> 23:50.800
And that is patti-vedan, another word for you, patti-vedan.

23:50.800 --> 23:59.680
The literal meaning is piercing, penetrating.

23:59.680 --> 24:08.600
You develop your samadhi in such a way that the mind gets concentrated by observing the

24:08.600 --> 24:16.280
reality that you are experiencing.

24:16.280 --> 24:26.360
The reality pertaining to yourself, pertaining to the mind-matter phenomena.

24:26.360 --> 24:34.880
You start working with respiration, which is related to both the mind and the matter.

24:34.880 --> 24:44.960
And as you proceed further, you notice that you have got a very large stock, a very big

24:44.960 --> 24:54.480
accumulation of complexes, of impurities deep inside.

24:54.480 --> 25:03.280
And although you are learning to control your mind, although you try to abstain from unwholesome

25:03.320 --> 25:11.560
physical and vocal actions, yet from time to time, these accumulated impurities come

25:11.560 --> 25:19.980
up on the surface and you get overwhelmed again, you are overpowered.

25:19.980 --> 25:25.920
So you have to reach that depth to take those impurities out.

25:25.920 --> 25:31.840
And that is patti-vedan.

25:31.840 --> 25:40.160
You have to witness the truth at the deeper level.

25:40.160 --> 25:49.280
There is a truth, which we call panyatthi, the apparent truth.

25:49.280 --> 25:53.440
It appears to be so, this is the truth.

25:53.440 --> 25:58.160
It seems to be so, it appears to be so.

25:58.160 --> 26:11.920
This apparent truth has to be removed so that you are able to witness the ultimate truth.

26:11.920 --> 26:20.440
And this is possible if you remove the curtain, which does not allow you to witness the truth

26:20.440 --> 26:22.720
behind this curtain.

26:22.720 --> 26:30.920
The curtain of the apparent truth is a barrier.

26:30.920 --> 26:40.680
You have to cut asunder this curtain, pierce, penetrate, remove it.

26:40.680 --> 26:45.240
And this is what is vipashyana.

26:45.240 --> 26:50.600
We keep on giving explanation of vipashyana in these words.

27:02.600 --> 27:11.440
Removing the apparent truth, removing the curtain of the apparent truth, you start moving

27:11.440 --> 27:14.880
towards the ultimate truth.

27:14.880 --> 27:21.960
The ultimate truth pertaining to this material structure, which you keep on saying I, I,

27:21.960 --> 27:27.520
mine, mine, myself.

27:27.520 --> 27:32.500
The ultimate truth pertaining to the mental structure, the mind.

27:32.500 --> 27:40.600
The ultimate truth pertaining to the mental contents, which you keep on saying I, I, mine,

27:40.760 --> 27:45.320
mine, myself, myself.

27:45.320 --> 28:00.480
And beyond this mind and matter, the ultimate truth of nibbana, the eternal truth, beyond

28:00.480 --> 28:05.360
the entire field of mind and matter.

28:06.120 --> 28:11.240
And this is possible only by this pativetan.

28:11.240 --> 28:18.620
Moving piercingly, penetratingly, piercingly, penetratingly, the apparent truth, which has

28:18.620 --> 28:31.960
manifested itself in a very solidified way, intensified way, dividing it, dissecting it,

28:32.560 --> 28:36.800
disintegrating it, dissolving, dissolving, dissolving.

28:36.800 --> 28:44.040
You move towards the ultimate truth, ultimate truth pertaining to the matter, ultimate truth

28:44.040 --> 28:48.680
pertaining to the mind, ultimate truth pertaining to the mental contents.

28:48.680 --> 28:56.640
And then piercingly, penetratingly, piercingly, penetratingly, you pierce the entire field

28:57.320 --> 29:04.320
of mind and matter, and then you can witness something which is beyond mind and matter.

29:04.320 --> 29:08.160
Pativetan.

29:08.160 --> 29:19.960
This practice of pativetan, the piercing panya, the piercing wisdom, which is vipassana, this

29:20.280 --> 29:28.400
takes one to the final goal of full liberation.

29:28.400 --> 29:35.480
Therefore these eight days when you will be listening to this satipatthana sutra, understand

29:35.480 --> 29:47.800
the purpose of hearing this sutra is to hear this pariyatthi is to get inspiration, to

29:47.800 --> 29:53.480
get guidance for the next step, patipatthi.

29:53.480 --> 30:04.480
And again to get inspiration, to get guidance, to take the next step, pativetan, pariyatthi

30:04.480 --> 30:09.840
is merely theoretical knowledge, which is very helpful no doubt, but that is not the

30:09.840 --> 30:11.960
end of it.

30:12.120 --> 30:23.480
Pariyatthi, patipatthi, pativetan, these three steps will cover the entire universe

30:23.480 --> 30:26.640
of wisdom.

30:26.640 --> 30:35.840
One who takes these three steps covers the entire universe of wisdom.

30:35.840 --> 30:40.880
These three steps have to be taken.

30:40.880 --> 30:53.520
This is what you keep on hearing in your discourses of ten days, sutamaya panya, chantamaya panya,

30:53.520 --> 31:02.480
and bhavanamaya panya, sutamaya panya.

31:02.480 --> 31:10.720
You heard, you heard something about wisdom, it is not your wisdom, somebody else's wisdom,

31:10.720 --> 31:22.280
you heard it, chantamaya panya, you used your intellect to understand it, you intellectualised

31:22.280 --> 31:30.960
whatever you heard, both of these are not your panya, not your wisdom, somebody else's

31:30.960 --> 31:40.120
wisdom you heard, you rationalised, both are very good.

31:40.120 --> 31:46.080
But they are very good only if you take the third step, bhavanamaya panya.

31:46.080 --> 31:53.040
Then you are witnessing the truth yourself, something is happening, and you are witnessing

31:53.040 --> 31:55.080
it.

31:55.080 --> 32:00.360
And you repeatedly keep on witnessing, keep on witnessing, this is how it develops, your

32:00.360 --> 32:06.280
own wisdom starts developing, developing, developing, and it is the bhavanamaya panya

32:06.360 --> 32:13.640
which takes you to the final goal.

32:13.640 --> 32:27.720
In another tradition, we have the same three steps using three different words for them.

32:27.720 --> 32:45.240
The first is sadh, sach, the truth of the word, the word is a truth, people who become

32:45.240 --> 32:58.840
very fanatical, who develop a lot of attachment to their scriptures without even understanding

32:58.840 --> 33:05.920
what it is, for them the word of the scripture is the truth.

33:05.920 --> 33:11.640
One must accept what the scripture says, whether you understand or not, whether you experience

33:11.640 --> 33:16.360
or not, whether you witness or not, this is the truth.

33:16.360 --> 33:20.800
The word said by an enlightened person is the truth.

33:20.800 --> 33:25.000
The word in a particular scripture is a truth.

33:25.000 --> 33:31.840
Yes, even if it is a truth, it is not for you.

33:31.840 --> 33:38.600
It is a truth for somebody who witnessed it, you only heard.

33:38.600 --> 33:42.560
And you developed attachment to it.

33:42.560 --> 33:58.280
This is first sadh, sach, and the next anumana sach, now you start understanding it at the

33:58.920 --> 34:11.880
level by inference, oh it is so, oh that means it must be like this, anumana, you see some

34:11.880 --> 34:19.560
smoke somewhere, oh there is smoke, so certainly there must be fire, you have not seen fire,

34:19.560 --> 34:33.320
you have seen smoke, and then you intellectualise it, inference, there must be fire.

34:33.320 --> 34:41.920
Both of these can be illusionary, can be delusionary.

34:41.920 --> 34:52.040
The third, pachakha sach, pachakha, you witness now, you directly witness the truth yourself

34:52.040 --> 35:01.960
and that truth is the real truth for you, that is going to help you.

35:01.960 --> 35:12.880
The entire teaching of an enlightened person is to inspire you so that you witness the

35:12.880 --> 35:23.120
truth yourself directly, merely believing in what a Buddha said will not lead you to

35:23.120 --> 35:29.760
the final goal, it is essential, it is helpful, no doubt, but unless you witness yourself

35:29.760 --> 35:36.240
to the ultimate truth, you can never be liberated.

35:36.240 --> 35:42.780
One who witnessed it became an enlightened person, became a Buddha, everyone has to witness

35:42.780 --> 35:50.880
the truth oneself to become an enlightened person, to become a liberated person.

35:51.800 --> 36:02.680
With this understanding, you will be going through this satipatthana sutra.

36:02.680 --> 36:12.200
Every word of this sutra should generate inspiration in you, should give you proper guidance, you

36:12.200 --> 36:21.000
listen to the sutra, you understand it at the intellectual level, but at the same time

36:21.000 --> 36:28.600
you have to witness, every teaching of an enlightened person has to be witnessed by

36:28.600 --> 36:33.600
one who aspires to get liberated.

36:34.600 --> 36:44.600
Unless you witness yourself, you will not get liberated.

36:44.600 --> 36:49.600
This is what is taught in satipatthana sutra.

36:49.600 --> 37:03.400
Sati, the word sati means aware, you are aware, because you are witnessing it.

37:04.400 --> 37:17.400
You are aware, every reality within the framework of the body, every reality pertaining to the

37:17.400 --> 37:27.400
matter, every reality pertaining to the mind, you are aware, you are aware.

37:27.400 --> 37:38.400
But you are aware with proper understanding also, with proper wisdom also.

37:38.400 --> 37:45.400
Then only satipatthana is satipatthana.

37:46.400 --> 38:01.400
Thana is getting established, your awareness gets established, patthana, in a proper way.

38:01.400 --> 38:14.400
In different ways, pakarena is patthana, and when you practice vipashana, when you practice

38:14.400 --> 38:21.400
panya, we say pakarena, yaaneti, tipanya.

38:21.400 --> 38:30.400
From different angles, you understand the reality, and then it is panya for you.

38:30.400 --> 38:37.400
If you witness the reality only from one angle, then what you are witnessing is only a partial

38:37.400 --> 38:45.400
truth, and partial truth is distorted truth.

38:45.400 --> 38:50.400
It can create difficulty for you.

38:50.400 --> 38:57.400
You have to try and observe, witness the totality of the truth, and that will be possible from

38:57.400 --> 39:04.400
different angles, pakarena, and then it becomes panya, it becomes wisdom.

39:04.400 --> 39:15.400
So this sati, when it is joined with panya, then it becomes patthana.

39:15.400 --> 39:24.400
Therefore, with every time Buddha says sati, sato, he uses the word sampajano.

39:24.400 --> 39:27.400
When we go through the text, we will come to it.

39:27.400 --> 39:32.400
Sampajano, atapi, sampajano, satima.

39:32.400 --> 39:40.400
The sati, the awareness, the witnessing is perfect only when panya is there, when wisdom

39:40.400 --> 39:48.400
is there, when you can understand at the experiential level the nature of the reality which is manifesting

39:48.400 --> 39:50.400
itself.

39:50.400 --> 39:58.400
Its basic characteristic, the characteristic of anicca, look, arising, passing, arising,

39:58.400 --> 40:09.400
passing, the characteristic of dukkha, look, how very misery, misery is there.

40:09.400 --> 40:14.400
Even you experience something very pleasant, by the practice of panya, by the practice

40:14.400 --> 40:21.400
of vipashyana, it becomes so clear that look, this also is misery, there is inherent misery

40:21.400 --> 40:26.400
in it because it is not permanent.

40:26.400 --> 40:30.400
Every pleasant experience changes into an unpleasant situation.

40:30.400 --> 40:33.400
The law of nature is such.

40:33.400 --> 40:36.400
So miseries are not there.

40:36.400 --> 40:42.400
And with every pleasant experience that you have, the tendency is to develop attachment

40:42.400 --> 40:43.400
towards it.

40:43.400 --> 40:46.400
You start clinging to it.

40:46.400 --> 40:49.400
And when it is gone, because it is anicca, it is bound to go away.

40:49.400 --> 40:52.400
And when it goes away, you feel so miserable.

40:52.400 --> 40:55.400
That you will understand by your own experience.

40:55.400 --> 41:00.400
So it is dukkha, dukkha, dukkha.

41:00.400 --> 41:06.400
Whatever you experience within the framework of the body is nothing but dukkha, dukkha,

41:06.400 --> 41:08.400
dukkha.

41:08.400 --> 41:12.400
This is not a philosophy.

41:12.400 --> 41:21.400
This is the truth which one has to experience by pativedhan, pativedhan, dukkha, dukkha.

41:21.400 --> 41:28.400
And then by this pativedhan, dividing, dissecting, disintegrating, dividing, dissecting, disintegrating,

41:28.400 --> 41:40.400
dissolving, dissolving, one comes to the stage where one witnesses that this solidified

41:40.400 --> 41:49.400
material structure, this body is actually nothing but subatomic particles, kalapa, kalapa.

41:49.400 --> 41:53.400
There is no solidity in it.

41:53.400 --> 41:58.400
One reaches the stage of bhanga, total dissolution.

41:58.400 --> 42:04.400
Every kalapa, every subatomic particle is arising, passing, arising, passing, arising,

42:04.400 --> 42:05.400
passing.

42:05.400 --> 42:11.400
And so also the mind manifests itself many a times in a very solidified way.

42:11.400 --> 42:16.400
The contents of the mind manifest themselves in a very solidified way.

42:16.400 --> 42:23.400
Very solidified emotion as a reason, anger as a reason, fear as a reason, passion as

42:23.400 --> 42:25.400
a reason.

42:25.400 --> 42:32.400
So intensified, so solidified, you get overwhelmed, you get overpowered.

42:32.400 --> 42:34.400
Vipashyana helps you.

42:34.400 --> 42:37.400
Pativedhan helps you.

42:37.400 --> 42:41.400
The penetrating, the piercing panya starts helping you.

42:41.400 --> 42:46.400
You divide, you dissect, you disintegrate, you divide, you dissect, you disintegrate.

42:46.400 --> 42:52.400
And this is the stage where you find that however intense this emotion might have been,

42:52.400 --> 42:57.400
it is nothing but wavelets, wavelets, wavelets.

42:57.400 --> 43:00.400
Material structure is wavelet, wavelet, wavelet.

43:00.400 --> 43:03.400
The mental structure is wavelet, wavelet, wavelet.

43:03.400 --> 43:08.400
The mental contents are wavelets, wavelets, wavelets.

43:08.400 --> 43:12.400
All anicca, anicca, anicca.

43:12.400 --> 43:15.400
Then it becomes clear.

43:15.400 --> 43:17.400
What is I?

43:17.400 --> 43:20.400
Is this material structure I?

43:20.400 --> 43:23.400
Is this mental structure I?

43:23.400 --> 43:26.400
Are these mental contents I?

43:26.400 --> 43:28.400
Are they mine?

43:28.400 --> 43:31.400
Do I really possess them?

43:31.400 --> 43:34.400
And the whole mind, matter, structure, it is myself?

43:34.400 --> 43:37.400
Is it myself?

43:37.400 --> 43:39.400
And it becomes so clear.

43:39.400 --> 43:43.400
For conventional purpose, we have to use these words.

43:43.400 --> 43:48.400
Actually there is no I, no mind, no myself.

43:48.400 --> 43:53.400
Just this mind-matter phenomena, interaction of mind and matter,

43:53.400 --> 43:58.400
a constant interaction of mind and matter,

43:58.400 --> 44:01.400
the mind influencing the matter,

44:01.400 --> 44:06.400
the matter influencing the mind,

44:06.400 --> 44:13.400
the mind becomes a cause for the arising of matter,

44:13.400 --> 44:17.400
the matter becomes a cause for the arising of mind.

44:17.400 --> 44:20.400
How these currents are going on within me,

44:20.400 --> 44:23.400
these cross currents, these undercurrents,

44:23.400 --> 44:26.400
and this is what I am saying I,

44:26.400 --> 44:28.400
this is what I say mind,

44:28.400 --> 44:31.400
this is what I say myself.

44:31.400 --> 44:33.400
It becomes clear.

44:33.400 --> 44:36.400
It becomes clear at the experiential level,

44:36.400 --> 44:39.400
then it is anatta,

44:39.400 --> 44:42.400
this anicca, impermanence,

44:42.400 --> 44:45.400
dukkha, misery, anatta,

44:45.400 --> 44:48.400
selflessness,

44:48.400 --> 44:51.400
egolessness,

44:51.400 --> 44:53.400
is not a philosophy,

44:53.400 --> 44:58.400
is not to be taken as a philosophy, sectarian philosophy.

44:58.400 --> 45:03.400
This is not applicable only to those who call themselves Buddhist,

45:03.400 --> 45:05.400
nothing doing.

45:05.400 --> 45:07.400
This is applicable to everyone.

45:07.400 --> 45:10.400
One may call oneself a Hindu or a Muslim or a Christian or a Jewish,

45:10.400 --> 45:12.400
it makes no difference.

45:12.400 --> 45:16.400
One may be black or white or brown or yellow, it makes no difference.

45:16.400 --> 45:19.400
One may be a man or a woman, it makes no difference.

45:19.400 --> 45:23.400
Everybody is just a bundle of mind and matter

45:23.400 --> 45:26.400
and constant interaction going on

45:26.400 --> 45:29.400
and without knowing what is happening inside,

45:29.400 --> 45:31.400
one develops this I,

45:31.400 --> 45:33.400
I,

45:33.400 --> 45:35.400
this ego, this false ego,

45:35.400 --> 45:38.400
then tremendous amount of attachment to this false ego,

45:38.400 --> 45:41.400
which brings nothing but misery.

45:41.400 --> 45:43.400
All this is law of nature,

45:43.400 --> 45:45.400
which will become so clear,

45:45.400 --> 45:50.400
and it will become clear only by pati ve dhan.

45:50.400 --> 45:53.400
The third step, piercing,

45:53.400 --> 45:56.400
penetrating, piercing, penetrating,

45:56.400 --> 46:00.400
the panya piercing, penetrating, piercing, penetrating.

46:00.400 --> 46:07.400
So sati, if the awareness is not with this piercing, penetrating panya,

46:07.400 --> 46:11.400
then mere awareness will not help you.

46:11.400 --> 46:15.400
Then you will always remain aware of the apparent truth

46:15.400 --> 46:18.400
and you can't understand what the ultimate truth is,

46:18.400 --> 46:21.400
what the real truth is.

46:22.400 --> 46:25.400
The awareness is there,

46:25.400 --> 46:28.400
very good awareness is there.

46:31.400 --> 46:34.400
With a circus girl,

46:34.400 --> 46:40.400
who is walking on a tightrope,

46:40.400 --> 46:45.400
she is so much aware of every step she takes,

46:45.400 --> 46:50.400
little awareness and she may fall down.

46:50.400 --> 46:53.400
Her life is in danger.

46:53.400 --> 46:56.400
Parts of her body are in danger.

46:56.400 --> 46:59.400
So she has to be very aware.

46:59.400 --> 47:03.400
But this awareness does not make her an arhant, far away,

47:03.400 --> 47:06.400
not even a sotapanna, far away,

47:06.400 --> 47:10.400
because she can't understand what is going on inside.

47:10.400 --> 47:13.400
She is only with the apparent truth.

47:13.400 --> 47:17.400
Similarly, a dancer,

47:17.400 --> 47:19.400
dancing on the platform,

47:19.400 --> 47:21.400
she is so aware of every step,

47:21.400 --> 47:25.400
every movement of every limb of her body.

47:25.400 --> 47:29.400
Just aware, aware of the apparent truth.

47:29.400 --> 47:31.400
Panya is missing.

47:31.400 --> 47:35.400
Sati is not perfect without panya.

47:35.400 --> 47:39.400
Satipatthana is sati with panya.

47:39.400 --> 47:44.400
You won't get established in the awareness with wisdom.

47:44.400 --> 47:49.400
Wisdom of anicca, arising, passing, arising, passing,

47:49.400 --> 47:52.400
or dukkha, misery, or anatta,

47:52.400 --> 47:55.400
no I, no mine, no myself,

47:55.400 --> 48:01.400
and all that at the experiential level.

48:04.400 --> 48:10.400
The discourse of satipatthana is for that purpose.

48:10.400 --> 48:15.400
Sati plays a very important part

48:15.400 --> 48:19.400
in the practice of dhamma,

48:21.400 --> 48:25.400
in witnessing the truth.

48:27.400 --> 48:31.400
We have been talking about five friends

48:31.400 --> 48:37.400
in our usual discourses of ordinary ten-day courses.

48:38.400 --> 48:44.400
Saddha, Veerya, Sati, Samadhi, Panya.

48:44.400 --> 48:48.400
The five friends,

48:48.400 --> 48:54.400
your faith, devotion,

48:54.400 --> 48:58.400
and your effort, and your awareness,

48:58.400 --> 49:01.400
and your concentration,

49:01.400 --> 49:03.400
and your wisdom, your panya.

49:03.400 --> 49:06.400
These are your five friends.

49:07.400 --> 49:13.400
In the words of Buddha, they are called five indriyas.

49:16.400 --> 49:22.400
The word indra means the ruler, the king.

49:22.400 --> 49:27.400
The king of the celestial world is called indra,

49:27.400 --> 49:31.400
the ruler, the master.

49:31.400 --> 49:36.400
So indriya, there are two types of indriyas.

49:36.400 --> 49:44.400
One indriya is the sensitors, eyes, ears, nose, tongue, and the body.

49:44.400 --> 49:48.400
They are indriyas. They are also called indriya. Why?

49:48.400 --> 49:52.400
Because they keep on mastering us, they keep on overpowering us.

49:52.400 --> 49:55.400
Every now and then we find that we have become slaves

49:55.400 --> 49:59.400
of one or the other of these five sensitors.

49:59.400 --> 50:01.400
So they are called indriya.

50:01.400 --> 50:05.400
So also these five faculties, they are called indriya

50:05.400 --> 50:10.400
because we become masters of those five faculties.

50:10.400 --> 50:16.400
And sati is one of those faculties, awareness, awareness.

50:16.400 --> 50:20.400
These five indriyas, in the language of those days,

50:20.400 --> 50:25.400
in the words of Buddha, were also called five bala.

50:25.400 --> 50:28.400
Bala means force, strength.

50:28.400 --> 50:32.400
These five are our strength.

50:32.400 --> 50:37.400
For every meditator, for everyone who walks on the path of liberation,

50:37.400 --> 50:42.400
these five are very important strengths.

50:42.400 --> 50:47.400
And sati is one amongst them.

50:47.400 --> 50:51.400
Sati is so important.

50:51.400 --> 50:58.400
And then you might have heard the seven bojhangas,

50:58.400 --> 51:02.400
the seven factors of enlightenment.

51:02.400 --> 51:08.400
Amongst those seven factors of enlightenment, sati is one.

51:08.400 --> 51:11.400
And a very important one.

51:11.400 --> 51:15.400
You are aware. With every factor of enlightenment,

51:15.400 --> 51:18.400
you start with awareness, and you are aware, you are aware,

51:18.400 --> 51:21.400
you are aware of every factor of enlightenment

51:21.400 --> 51:25.400
till you reach the final goal of enlightenment.

51:25.400 --> 51:28.400
Sati is so important.

51:28.400 --> 51:36.400
But sati is important and fruitful if we make use of it properly.

51:36.400 --> 51:48.400
And that is what you will be understanding from the words of Buddha.

51:49.400 --> 51:57.400
The sutra, that means the teaching of Satipatthana.

51:57.400 --> 52:03.400
Tomorrow we will start reading this sutra.

52:03.400 --> 52:12.400
Today this background for you to understand

52:12.400 --> 52:18.400
that the most important thing is taking steps on the path,

52:18.400 --> 52:23.400
piercingly, penetratingly, moving towards the ultimate truth.

52:23.400 --> 52:28.400
Tearing away the apparent truth and moving towards the ultimate truth.

52:28.400 --> 52:32.400
And this is what you do by practicing vipashyana.

52:32.400 --> 52:37.400
Little by little, step by step, you keep on dividing, dissecting,

52:37.400 --> 52:41.400
disintegrating, dissolving, and moving from the apparent truth

52:41.400 --> 52:44.400
towards the ultimate truth.

52:44.400 --> 52:56.400
Therefore, just reading these sutras or hearing these sutras,

52:56.400 --> 53:02.400
the discourses should not become the aim of the life.

53:02.400 --> 53:07.400
There is a big danger there.

53:07.400 --> 53:10.400
We have to be very careful.

53:10.400 --> 53:15.400
All those who are running such vipashyana centers now,

53:15.400 --> 53:19.400
and all those who will be running such vipashyana centers in future,

53:19.400 --> 53:24.400
for centuries, they have to be very careful.

53:24.400 --> 53:29.400
That a vipashyana center is a vipashyana center.

53:29.400 --> 53:36.400
The purpose of vipashyana center is patipatti and pativedan.

53:36.400 --> 53:43.400
The actual practice to develop bhavanamaya panya,

53:43.400 --> 53:48.400
your own wisdom which you witness yourself,

53:48.400 --> 53:54.400
from the grossest to the subtlest, your own wisdom,

53:54.400 --> 54:01.400
the wisdom that you develop, that you multiply by your own experience.

54:01.400 --> 54:08.400
This is the purpose of such vipashyana centers.

54:08.400 --> 54:13.400
How vipashyana got lost?

54:13.400 --> 54:18.400
One reason out of so many others was

54:18.400 --> 54:24.400
that people started giving importance only

54:24.400 --> 54:27.400
to the theoretical part of it.

54:27.400 --> 54:32.400
Just the sutras, the discourses of Buddha.

54:32.400 --> 54:38.400
One feels so satisfied having recited the discourse of Buddha,

54:38.400 --> 54:42.400
having recited the entire tepidika,

54:42.400 --> 54:46.400
memorizing the entire tepidika.

54:46.400 --> 54:50.400
One feels so satisfied.

54:50.400 --> 54:54.400
Oh, the purpose of my life is fulfilled.

54:54.400 --> 54:58.400
Then, having discussions, debates, arguments,

54:58.400 --> 55:01.400
the meaning of this word is this, not that.

55:01.400 --> 55:04.400
No, no, it is that, not this.

55:04.400 --> 55:07.400
Centuries after centuries, this is what remained.

55:07.400 --> 55:10.400
The practice was lost.

55:10.400 --> 55:12.400
Confusion prevailed.

55:12.400 --> 55:17.400
Without practice you can't understand the words of an enlightened person.

55:17.400 --> 55:21.400
His words are words of his own experience.

55:21.400 --> 55:25.400
He is not writing scripture for the sake of writing scripture.

55:25.400 --> 55:29.400
He is not giving discourse for the sake of giving discourse.

55:29.400 --> 55:31.400
He is guiding people.

55:31.400 --> 55:34.400
This is how I have witnessed the truth,

55:34.400 --> 55:37.400
and this is how you have to witness the truth.

55:37.400 --> 55:40.400
And if you stop witnessing the truth,

55:40.400 --> 55:43.400
and if you start playing games with these words,

55:43.400 --> 55:46.400
the discourse is of Buddha,

55:46.400 --> 55:49.400
that will become a very big hindrance.

55:49.400 --> 55:55.400
Therefore, a Vipassana center is only for meditation.

55:55.400 --> 55:57.400
We make use of these words,

55:57.400 --> 56:01.400
like we are going to make use now for this next one week.

56:01.400 --> 56:04.400
We read the words of Buddha,

56:04.400 --> 56:08.400
understand to get inspiration, to get guidance,

56:08.400 --> 56:10.400
what Buddha wanted us to do,

56:10.400 --> 56:13.400
how he wanted us to practice.

56:13.400 --> 56:18.400
But actual practice always will remain predominant,

56:18.400 --> 56:23.400
because without practice we can't reach the final goal.

56:23.400 --> 56:29.400
Again, it should be understood that we are not denouncing Paryatthe.

56:29.400 --> 56:32.400
We are not against the scriptures.

56:32.400 --> 56:34.400
We are not against the words of Buddha.

56:34.400 --> 56:37.400
How can one be against the words of Buddha,

56:37.400 --> 56:40.400
one who is practicing what Buddha taught,

56:40.400 --> 56:42.400
how can he be against the words of Buddha?

56:42.400 --> 56:45.400
But the words of Buddha should not become

56:45.400 --> 56:48.400
like the final goal of our life.

56:48.400 --> 56:52.400
Practice should remain the final goal.

56:52.400 --> 56:57.400
We are of course very thankful,

56:57.400 --> 57:02.400
we are of course very grateful

57:02.400 --> 57:06.400
to the Sangha,

57:06.400 --> 57:13.400
who has maintained the purity of the words of Buddha.

57:13.400 --> 57:19.400
There were some who maintained the purity of the practice,

57:19.400 --> 57:22.400
as taught by Buddha, the Vipassana.

57:22.400 --> 57:24.400
We are very grateful to them,

57:24.400 --> 57:28.400
because because of them we got this wonderful technique,

57:28.400 --> 57:31.400
otherwise it would have been long lost,

57:31.400 --> 57:33.400
as it got lost in many places.

57:33.400 --> 57:37.400
At least one tradition maintained it in its original purity,

57:37.400 --> 57:39.400
that's how we got it.

57:39.400 --> 57:48.400
Similarly, we developed great feeling of gratitude towards those,

57:48.400 --> 57:51.400
who might have practiced or might not have practiced,

57:51.400 --> 57:54.400
but at least they maintained the words of Buddha,

57:54.400 --> 57:58.400
from generation to generation, from generation to generation,

57:58.400 --> 58:00.400
for the last 25 centuries,

58:00.400 --> 58:03.400
from teacher to pupil, from teacher to pupil,

58:03.400 --> 58:06.400
they maintained these words.

58:06.400 --> 58:09.400
And that is how we can compare now,

58:09.400 --> 58:12.400
because questions keep arising,

58:12.400 --> 58:15.400
whether what we are practicing,

58:15.400 --> 58:19.400
is it really the teaching of Buddha?

58:19.400 --> 58:22.400
Did really Buddha wanted us to work like this?

58:22.400 --> 58:25.400
Now how to prove that it is so?

58:25.400 --> 58:32.400
It is only the words which are maintained in its pristine purity by this school,

58:32.400 --> 58:39.400
who felt that they are responsible for keeping the words of Buddha intact,

58:39.400 --> 58:43.400
and that is why they are called Dhamma-Bhandagarika,

58:43.400 --> 58:48.400
they are like treasures,

58:48.400 --> 58:52.400
keeping the words of Buddha quite safe,

58:52.400 --> 58:57.400
from generation to generation, from generation to generation.

58:57.400 --> 59:00.400
We are thankful to them.

59:00.400 --> 59:02.400
Let both be joined together.

59:02.400 --> 59:05.400
We understand the words of Buddha,

59:05.400 --> 59:08.400
and we practice.

59:08.400 --> 59:10.400
We understand the words of Buddha,

59:10.400 --> 59:13.400
and we practice.

59:13.400 --> 59:16.400
Then we get so much confidence in our practice.

59:16.400 --> 59:20.400
I am practicing as Buddha wanted me to practice.

59:20.400 --> 59:23.400
I am practicing in the right way.

59:23.400 --> 59:26.400
I am practicing in the proper way.

59:26.400 --> 59:29.400
These seven days,

59:29.400 --> 59:32.400
we will make use of this particular sutra.

59:32.400 --> 59:34.400
Later on,

59:34.400 --> 59:38.400
it is not necessary that every student

59:38.400 --> 59:42.400
must study the entire Tipitaka, all the words of Buddha.

59:42.400 --> 59:44.400
Not necessary.

59:44.400 --> 59:48.400
If someone finds time to go through all that,

59:48.400 --> 59:52.400
wonderful, every word as I say is like a nectar,

59:52.400 --> 59:55.400
and for a Vipassana meditator, every word is

59:55.400 --> 59:58.400
like a guidance being given by Buddha,

59:58.400 --> 01:00:01.400
as if he is saying these words to me, for my purpose.

01:00:01.400 --> 01:00:02.400
To me he is guiding.

01:00:02.400 --> 01:00:04.400
Hey, you work like this.

01:00:04.400 --> 01:00:06.400
Hey, you understand like this.

01:00:06.400 --> 01:00:09.400
It will become so clear, so inspiring.

01:00:09.400 --> 01:00:12.400
But yet I say it is not necessary.

01:00:12.400 --> 01:00:18.400
Even a few sutras one has properly understood, good enough.

01:00:18.400 --> 01:00:21.400
Buddha says that even one gatha, even two lines,

01:00:21.400 --> 01:00:23.400
if you understood properly,

01:00:23.400 --> 01:00:25.400
and you work according to that,

01:00:25.400 --> 01:00:28.400
good enough to take you to the final goal.

01:00:28.400 --> 01:00:33.400
One literal meaning of this word pariyatti is,

01:00:33.400 --> 01:00:38.400
in Sanskrit or Hindi we say pariyatti, sufficient.

01:00:38.400 --> 01:00:42.400
What is sufficient for you to get inspiration and work

01:00:42.400 --> 01:00:45.400
and reach the final goal is pariyatti.

01:00:45.400 --> 01:00:48.400
It can be sufficient, one sutra should be sufficient for you

01:00:48.400 --> 01:00:50.400
to take you to the final goal.

01:00:50.400 --> 01:00:54.400
Even one gatha, one verse will be sufficient to take you to the final goal.

01:00:54.400 --> 01:01:00.400
For some larger, more number of discourses will be sufficient

01:01:00.400 --> 01:01:04.400
to give them inspiration to reach the final goal.

01:01:04.400 --> 01:01:09.400
But final goal will be reached only when you take steps on the path.

01:01:09.400 --> 01:01:17.400
Therefore a warning for everyone who manages such Vipashyana centres,

01:01:17.400 --> 01:01:22.400
here, around the world, now and in future,

01:01:22.400 --> 01:01:28.400
that practice of Vipashyana will remain the main teaching here,

01:01:28.400 --> 01:01:33.400
the main activity here, and the words of Buddha,

01:01:33.400 --> 01:01:36.400
like you get evening discourses.

01:01:36.400 --> 01:01:42.400
Every course you go to evening discourse to understand how you must practice,

01:01:42.400 --> 01:01:44.400
which is the proper way of practice.

01:01:44.400 --> 01:01:47.400
And why we are practicing in this way?

01:01:47.400 --> 01:01:50.400
To understand it at the intellectual level,

01:01:50.400 --> 01:01:56.400
and to develop great confidence in whatever step you are taking

01:01:56.400 --> 01:02:01.400
for that purpose these evening discourses, and for that purpose the pariyatti.

01:02:01.400 --> 01:02:06.400
Such centres can take up a few sutras, a few discourses,

01:02:06.400 --> 01:02:11.400
and discuss in the evening discourses so that people understand.

01:02:11.400 --> 01:02:16.400
But that should not become the main aim.

01:02:16.400 --> 01:02:22.400
Otherwise these meditation centres will become pariyatti centres,

01:02:22.400 --> 01:02:26.400
where all the Tipitikas will be taught and people will be just discussing

01:02:26.400 --> 01:02:30.400
and reciting and debating and reciting, playing emotional games,

01:02:30.400 --> 01:02:35.400
devotional games, playing intellectual games, but not practicing.

01:02:35.400 --> 01:02:38.400
It will be a great misfortune.

01:02:38.400 --> 01:02:41.400
That should not be allowed to happen.

01:02:41.400 --> 01:02:45.400
So understand, these seven days from tomorrow evening,

01:02:45.400 --> 01:02:47.400
when we are reciting this sutra,

01:02:47.400 --> 01:02:52.400
it will be to understand the practical aspect of it properly.

01:02:52.400 --> 01:02:58.400
To understand the patipatti, to understand the pativedhan properly.

01:02:58.400 --> 01:03:04.400
Every step that we take on the path, let us understand it properly,

01:03:04.400 --> 01:03:10.400
so that we do not get diverted to something else.

01:03:10.400 --> 01:03:13.400
No deviation. We remain on the right path,

01:03:13.400 --> 01:03:16.400
the straight path which takes us to the final goal.

01:03:16.400 --> 01:03:21.400
Without wasting our time here and there on some side issues,

01:03:21.400 --> 01:03:23.400
we are on the path.

01:03:23.400 --> 01:03:27.400
Just to understand it properly, this recitation every evening,

01:03:27.400 --> 01:03:30.400
the understanding of the words of Buddha every evening,

01:03:30.400 --> 01:03:34.400
but the practice will remain the same.

01:03:34.400 --> 01:03:38.400
Now you are on anapanas.

01:03:38.400 --> 01:03:44.400
Keep on giving your time to the observation of respiration,

01:03:44.400 --> 01:03:48.400
the truth of the breath coming in, going out.

01:03:48.400 --> 01:03:52.400
This is sati. You are witnessing it.

01:03:52.400 --> 01:03:55.400
This is not merely because the book says so.

01:03:55.400 --> 01:03:58.400
This is not merely because your teacher says so.

01:03:58.400 --> 01:04:00.400
This is not merely because Buddha said so.

01:04:00.400 --> 01:04:04.400
This is nature. This is the nature of a living person.

01:04:04.400 --> 01:04:07.400
We are alive. So the breath is there.

01:04:07.400 --> 01:04:12.400
And I am witnessing this breath coming in, going out,

01:04:12.400 --> 01:04:16.400
coming in, going out, as it is.

01:04:16.400 --> 01:04:19.400
I am not making it a breathing exercise.

01:04:19.400 --> 01:04:21.400
I am not doing anything to regulate it.

01:04:21.400 --> 01:04:24.400
Just observing. Just observing.

01:04:24.400 --> 01:04:28.400
And as I observe, as I observe, as I witness, as I witness,

01:04:28.400 --> 01:04:31.400
as I witness my mind gets concentrated, concentrated.

01:04:31.400 --> 01:04:36.400
Naturally, the breath becomes finer and finer, shorter and shorter.

01:04:36.400 --> 01:04:39.400
Till it reaches the stage where it makes a U-turn,

01:04:39.400 --> 01:04:42.400
as it comes out, so it starts entering in, as it comes out,

01:04:42.400 --> 01:04:45.400
so it starts entering in. And you are aware of it.

01:04:45.400 --> 01:04:48.400
You do nothing. You are aware of it.

01:04:48.400 --> 01:04:51.400
And at times you feel as if it has stopped.

01:04:51.400 --> 01:04:55.400
And then again you feel some hunger for the oxygen,

01:04:55.400 --> 01:04:57.400
and again a big breath comes.

01:04:57.400 --> 01:05:01.400
And again you are aware of it. It becomes shorter, shorter, shorter, shorter.

01:05:01.400 --> 01:05:04.400
It starts making a U-turn here. You feel it has stopped.

01:05:04.400 --> 01:05:06.400
And again a big breath will come.

01:05:06.400 --> 01:05:09.400
So if it's a big breath, you are aware. It's a big breath. It's a long breath.

01:05:09.400 --> 01:05:12.400
If it's a short breath, you are aware. It's a short breath. It's a short breath.

01:05:12.400 --> 01:05:17.400
You are just aware. You are aware of the reality as it is.

01:05:17.400 --> 01:05:21.400
Of course, at times when you can't feel the breath at all,

01:05:21.400 --> 01:05:23.400
it becomes so subtle.

01:05:23.400 --> 01:05:29.400
Then as usual you are permitted to take a few breaths intentionally, consciously,

01:05:29.400 --> 01:05:33.400
but that is just to help you to come to the stage

01:05:33.400 --> 01:05:37.400
where you start feeling the natural breath as it comes in, as it goes out,

01:05:37.400 --> 01:05:41.400
as it comes in, as it goes out.

01:05:41.400 --> 01:05:46.400
Understand your usual courses are for 10 days,

01:05:46.400 --> 01:05:50.400
and this Satipatthana course is only for 8 days.

01:05:51.400 --> 01:05:54.400
Time is short.

01:05:54.400 --> 01:05:58.400
You have to make use of this time more seriously.

01:05:58.400 --> 01:06:02.400
And being old students, you have got one wonderful advantage

01:06:02.400 --> 01:06:06.400
that in these usual, ordinary courses,

01:06:06.400 --> 01:06:11.400
you have quite a few number of new students

01:06:11.400 --> 01:06:16.400
which remain confused for a number of days what is happening.

01:06:16.400 --> 01:06:19.400
And they don't understand the value of discipline.

01:06:19.400 --> 01:06:22.400
They don't understand the value of silence.

01:06:22.400 --> 01:06:25.400
So they keep on disturbing.

01:06:25.400 --> 01:06:32.400
Now there are old students, matured students,

01:06:32.400 --> 01:06:37.400
having taken at least a couple of courses, maybe even more.

01:06:37.400 --> 01:06:41.400
So they understand how they have to work.

01:06:41.400 --> 01:06:45.400
And another thing that they understand which is very important is

01:06:45.400 --> 01:06:48.400
continuity is the secret of success.

01:06:48.400 --> 01:06:53.400
So far as this technique is concerned, continuity, continuity.

01:06:53.400 --> 01:06:58.400
You work for some time, and then you feel very lazy.

01:06:58.400 --> 01:07:03.400
You stop working, or you start roaming about, wandering about here and there.

01:07:03.400 --> 01:07:08.400
Or you lie down and sleep, and then after some time again you start.

01:07:08.400 --> 01:07:13.400
You work a little, and then you stop working, you work a little, you stop working.

01:07:13.400 --> 01:07:17.400
You can't reach the goal. Continuous, continuous.

01:07:17.400 --> 01:07:20.400
Of course, mind will wander away, and you can't bring it back.

01:07:20.400 --> 01:07:23.400
It wanders, you bring it back, it wanders, it brings it back.

01:07:23.400 --> 01:07:28.400
That is, your effort is continuous efforts, continuous efforts.

01:07:28.400 --> 01:07:36.400
Day and night, you have to work very seriously, day and night.

01:07:36.400 --> 01:07:44.400
There is no recess period for you.

01:07:44.400 --> 01:07:52.400
Even the times what are called recess periods, like from morning 6.30 to 8 o'clock,

01:07:52.400 --> 01:08:00.400
or day 11 to 1, and then 5 to 6, and night from 9 to 4.30 in the morning.

01:08:00.400 --> 01:08:04.400
There is also time for meditation, awareness.

01:08:04.400 --> 01:08:08.400
Satipatthana, sati must get established.

01:08:08.400 --> 01:08:11.400
Awareness must get established.

01:08:11.400 --> 01:08:14.400
So all the time you are aware, you are aware, you are aware.

01:08:14.400 --> 01:08:18.400
Now you are in Anapanas, you are aware of respiration, aware of respiration.

01:08:18.400 --> 01:08:22.400
Whether you are sitting or standing or walking or lying,

01:08:22.400 --> 01:08:27.400
whether you are bathing or washing, whether you are eating or drinking,

01:08:27.400 --> 01:08:31.400
or even when you are lying down, till the time you get deep sleep,

01:08:31.400 --> 01:08:38.400
you are aware of respiration, respiration, natural breath coming in, going out, coming in, going out.

01:08:39.400 --> 01:08:45.400
Day and night, only the period when you are in deep sleep,

01:08:45.400 --> 01:08:48.400
rest of the time you are aware, you are aware.

01:08:48.400 --> 01:08:51.400
This is how the awareness will get established.

01:08:51.400 --> 01:08:56.400
The sati will get patthana, patitha pita.

01:08:56.400 --> 01:08:59.400
It becomes established, well established.

01:08:59.400 --> 01:09:03.400
And when you switch over to be pashana,

01:09:03.400 --> 01:09:09.400
then all the time you are aware of anicca, anicca, anicca,

01:09:09.400 --> 01:09:12.400
arising, passing, arising, passing.

01:09:12.400 --> 01:09:15.400
Day and night again.

01:09:15.400 --> 01:09:19.400
All the rules are so important for you.

01:09:19.400 --> 01:09:23.400
It's a very rare opportunity for somebody to get a course like this

01:09:23.400 --> 01:09:27.400
where there are no new students, only old students are there.

01:09:27.400 --> 01:09:30.400
With least disturbance, everybody is so serious.

01:09:30.400 --> 01:09:34.400
You got this opportunity, you got this facility, make use of it.

01:09:34.400 --> 01:09:38.400
And get your awareness established with wisdom,

01:09:38.400 --> 01:09:44.400
so that you come nearer and nearer to the final goal.

01:09:44.400 --> 01:09:49.400
Make best use of this opportunity.

01:09:49.400 --> 01:09:52.400
Make best use of your time.

01:09:52.400 --> 01:09:56.400
Make best use of whatever facility is available here.

01:09:56.400 --> 01:10:02.400
And make best use of this wonderful dhamma, the wonderful technique

01:10:02.400 --> 01:10:10.400
for your own good, for your own benefit, for your own liberation.

01:10:10.400 --> 01:10:16.400
Liberation from the bondages, the shackles, the chains of craving,

01:10:16.400 --> 01:10:21.400
of aversion, of ignorance.

01:10:21.400 --> 01:10:30.400
To enjoy real peace, real harmony, real happiness.

01:10:30.400 --> 01:10:47.400
May all of you enjoy real peace, real harmony, real happiness, real happiness.

01:11:51.400 --> 01:12:14.400
You may take rest for about five minutes.

01:12:14.400 --> 01:12:18.400
Take rest with the awareness of respiration.

01:12:18.400 --> 01:12:21.400
Come back and sit and continue to work sitting.

01:12:21.400 --> 01:12:26.400
Awareness of respiration, awareness of respiration.

01:12:26.400 --> 01:12:32.400
Maintain the continuity, maintain the continuity.

01:12:32.400 --> 01:12:37.400
Now take rest, take rest.

